When the devteam releases a new version, I always change the playground
directory in the source tree to include the version number, so that
instead of /usr/games/lib/nethackdir I now have the game in
/usr/games/lib/nh343dir and I have nethackdir as a symlink pointing there
for external utilities.
I always do that and the earlier mentioned changes before the first
compilation of a new version. And after compilation I copy the existing
bones and save files to the playground of the new version.

And I don't apply patches before checking whether or not they affect save
and bones files, and I trust the wizard mode prompt for unlinking bones.

If I happen to accidentally lose a bones or save file, I kick my ass and
feel angry at myself for a while, then I go on living as before.
But I don't remember whether that has ever actually happened yet.
I think I may have lost one record or logfile long time ago and that was
somewhat frustrating..

